Z||000000||Smokin87||01-10-2001||08:58 AM||||Ive been haveing some power issues with my 87 GT.  there are(were) several problems, first it was bad ingnition timing.  fixed that- i think, then there was a clogged catalytic converter, fixed that.  now when i accelerate, it has power "surges" and "jolkts".  according to the repair manual it says i may have a bad EGR valve.  but i checked that, and that all seems to be working.  what can i do, what can i check.   another problem it might be is my timing, i timed it by ear, i cant see the timing marks because of belts and pullies on the 2.8.  does anyone know how i can see the timing marks.  and finally (this one i feel stupid about asking), but does a 2.8, auto, all stock, have a differential or possi rear?<BR>SOME ONE PLEASE HELP ME!!<BR>justin||||reg||8
Z||000001||FieroJoe||01-10-2001||10:54 AM||||someone please correct me if I am wrong, but I believe all Fiero's were posi.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||01-10-2001||11:46 AM||||None are posi.||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GTZ34||01-10-2001||12:07 PM||||The FWD transaxles are not posi but you may be experiencing torque direction being switch as a wheel 'finds' traction.  Does your car have enough power to turn the wheels and if so are your tires leaving tracks?  If you go to a parking lot and try this then inspect the tracks for consistency.  If your wheels are not spinning, then you have an inconsistency in the engine under load.  Bypass EGR for now (plug vacuum line) to take that out of the equation and start from there.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Smokin87||01-10-2001||12:21 PM||||i think my problem is that there is no vacume to the EGR valve.  and my tires spin...sometimes.  but still, what can i do?||||reg||9
